      "title": "Local Qwen model setup",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Download the local Qwen model and MMProj\n\nThe MiniMax H3 Prompt Enhancer expects both GGUF files in:\n\n`/workspace/ComfyUI/models/LLM/Qwen3.8`\n\nOpen a terminal in the pod and run:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /workspace/ComfyUI/models/LLM/Qwen3.8\n\nhf download theresa00l/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-FP8-Q4_K_M-GGUF \\\n  qwen3.8-27b-uncensored-fp8-q4_k_m.gguf \\\n  --local-dir /workspace/ComfyUI/models/LLM/Qwen3.8\n\nhf download unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF \\\n  mmproj-F16.gguf \\\n  --local-dir /workspace/ComfyUI/models/LLM/Qwen3.8\n```\n\nThe model and projector together require approximately 18 GB. Restart ComfyUI or refresh the node after downloading them.\n\n## Documentation available inside the pod\n\n1. Start the pod and wait until code-server is ready.\n2. In RunPod, select **Connect** and open the HTTP service on port **9000**. You can also use `https://<POD_ID>-9000.proxy.runpod.net`.\n3. Sign in with the `PASSWORD` environment variable configured for the pod.\n4. Open `/workspace/README.md` in the code-server Explorer.\n5. For the complete Qwen, MMProj and llama.cpp test instructions, open `/workspace/docs/provisioning/hf_vlm.md`."
      ],
